Fixed a `KeyError` crash in `semgrep mcp` startup that occurred when any tool was pre-disabled via its `*_DISABLED` environment variable (for example `SEMGREP_SCAN_REMOTE_DISABLED=true`) and was subsequently encountered by the hard-coded transport- or hosting-mode deregistration branch. `deregister_tools()` now removes internal tool entries with idempotent `dict.pop(name, None)` instead of `del`, so the cleanup no longer assumes a tool is still registered when its branch runs.
